.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
.env
.env.*

.wrangler/

dist/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# The GitHub remote is PUBLIC. These hold planning material, requirement
# transcripts quoting the operator, transcript-derived grade bands, cross-lane
# handoffs enumerating security exposure in other repositories, and unpublished
# message drafts. The Pages allowlist in tools/stage_site.py keeps them off the
# deployed site; this keeps them off github.com. Both are needed.
docs/*
writing/drafts/

# The one exception, added 2026-08-10. AGENTS.md is a PUBLIC file that names six
# contracts under docs/ as binding, and `git ls-files docs/` returned zero, so
# the repo's own map pointed at files nobody who clones it can read. ADRs are the
# half that is safe to publish: a decision, its alternatives, and its falsifier,
# with no operator transcript, no grades, and no cross-repo exposure. Requirements
# and planning stay ignored by the `docs/*` line above. Publishing an ADR does not
# put it on the site: tools/stage_site.py's SHIP list is default-deny and does not
# name docs/, so this affects github.com only.
!docs/adr/

# Local run records: gate verdicts, review artifacts quoting source lines, e2e
# reports, the duplicate-unit scratch file. tools/stage_site.py lists state/ as
# FORBIDDEN, but that allowlist only governs what reaches the Pages deploy. It
# does nothing about github.com, so without this line one `git add -A` publishes
# 18 files of local run history to a public repository.
state/

shots/

daemon/.key

daemon/node_modules/
daemon/bun.lock
daemon/.comfy-key
dist-writing/
